  .stat-inline {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    background: var(--surface2);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 3px 10px;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    vertical-align: middle;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<!-- ===== HEADER ===== -->
<div class="report-header">
  <div class="badge">Space Industry Intelligence · April 2026</div>
  <h1>Active Satellites in Earth Orbit<br>2026 Catalog Analysis</h1>
  <div class="subtitle">A data-driven examination of the 14,875 active spacecraft currently tracked by NORAD — covering orbital regimes, constellation composition, launch trends, and implications for space sustainability.</div>
  <div class="report-meta">
    <span><strong>Data Source:</strong> CelesTrak / NORAD TLE Catalog</span>
    <span><strong>EPOCH Range:</strong> Feb 26 – Mar 30, 2026</span>
    <span><strong>Rows:</strong> 14,875 active satellites</span>
    <span><strong>Audience:</strong> Space-industry analysts &amp; policy advisors</span>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ===== MAIN CONTAINER ===== -->
<div class="container">

  <!-- ===== SECTION 1: OVERVIEW ===== -->
  <div class="section" id="overview">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-number">1</span>
      <h2>Catalog Overview &amp; Key Figures</h2>
    </div>

    <!-- KPI Grid -->
    <div class="kpi-grid">
      <div class="kpi-card blue">
        <div class="kpi-label">Total Active Satellites</div>
        <div class="kpi-value">14,875</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">NORAD-tracked, as of Mar 2026</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi-card green">
        <div class="kpi-label">LEO Share</div>
        <div class="kpi-value">86.5%</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">12,860 of 14,875 satellites</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi-card orange">
        <div class="kpi-label">Starlink Constellation</div>
        <div class="kpi-value">10,083</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">67.8% of all active satellites</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi-card purple">
        <div class="kpi-label">Median Inclination</div>
        <div class="kpi-value">53.16°</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">Driven by Starlink orbital shells</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi-card red">
        <div class="kpi-label">Launched Since 2020</div>
        <div class="kpi-value">13,461</div>
        <div class="kpi-sub">90.5% of all active satellites</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="callout">
      <strong>Catalog context:</strong> This dataset captures 14,875 operationally active satellites whose TLE elements were refreshed between February 26 and March 30, 2026. The data skews heavily toward recently launched constellations: <strong>90.5% of active satellites were placed in orbit after January 1, 2020</strong>, reflecting the explosive expansion of broadband megaconstellations rather than a large historical fleet.
    </div>

    <div class="chart-grid-2">
      <div class="chart-card">
        <div class="chart-title">Orbital Parameter Summary Statistics</div>
        <div class="chart-subtitle">Descriptive statistics for key TLE-derived parameters (n = 14,875)</div>
        <table class="data-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Parameter</th>
              <th>Min</th>
              <th>Median</th>
              <th>Mean</th>
              <th>Max</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Mean Motion (rev/day)</strong></td>
              <td>0.28</td>
              <td>15.27</td>
              <td>14.33</td>
              <td>16.30</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Inclination (°)</strong></td>
              <td>0.00°</td>
              <td>53.16°</td>
              <td>60.04°</td>
              <td>149.6°</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Eccentricity</strong></td>
              <td>0.000001</td>
              <td>0.000156</td>
              <td>0.00229</td>
              <td>0.896</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="chart-card">
        <div class="chart-title">Eccentricity Classification</div>
        <div class="chart-subtitle">Orbit circularity breakdown across all 14,875 satellites</div>
        <canvas id="eccChart" height="160"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ===== SECTION 2: ORBITAL REGIMES ===== -->
  <div class="section" id="orbit-regime">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-number">2</span>
      <h2>Orbital Regime Classification</h2>
    </div>

    <p>Satellites are classified using <strong>MEAN_MOTION thresholds</strong>: LEO (&gt;14 rev/day, ~160–2,000 km), MEO (2.0–14.0 rev/day, ~2,000–35,000 km), GEO (0.9–1.1 rev/day, ~35,786 km), and HEO (eccentricity &gt;0.1 with mean motion &lt;2.0). Sub-GEO objects with near-circular orbits (&lt;0.9 rev/day) are classified as Super-GEO/Other.</p>

    <div class="chart-grid-2">
      <div class="chart-card">
        <div class="chart-title">Satellites by Orbital Regime</div>
        <div class="chart-subtitle">Count and share using MEAN_MOTION thresholds</div>
        <canvas id="orbitDonut" height="220"></canvas>
      </div>
      <div class="chart-card">
        <div class="chart-title">Orbital Regime Detail Table</div>
        <div class="chart-subtitle">Mean Motion thresholds applied consistently</div>
        <table class="data-table" style="margin-top:8px;">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Regime</th>
              <th>Threshold</th>
              <th>Count</th>
              <th>Share</th>
              <th>Visual</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><span class="orbit-badge badge-leo">LEO</span></td>
              <td>&gt; 14.0 rev/day</td>
              <td><strong>12,860</strong></td>
              <td>86.5%</td>
              <td><div class="bar-fill-wrap"><div class="bar-fill" style="width:86.5%;background:var(--accent2);"></div></div></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><span class="orbit-badge badge-meo">MEO</span></td>
              <td>2.0 – 14.0 rev/day</td>
              <td><strong>1,336</strong></td>
              <td>8.98%</td>
              <td><div class="bar-fill-wrap"><div class="bar-fill" style="width:9%;background:var(--accent5);"></div></div></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><span class="orbit-badge badge-geo">GEO</span></td>
              <td>0.9 – 1.1 rev/day</td>
              <td><strong>596</strong></td>
              <td>4.01%</td>
              <td><div class="bar-fill-wrap"><div class="bar-fill" style="width:4%;background:var(--accent4);"></div></div></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><span class="orbit-badge badge-other">Sub-GEO</span></td>
              <td>&lt; 0.9 rev/day, ecc ≤ 0.1</td>
              <td><strong>64</strong></td>
              <td>0.43%</td>
              <td><div class="bar-fill-wrap"><div class="bar-fill" style="width:0.4%;background:var(--text-secondary);"></div></div></td>
            </tr>
